  "applies_to": "INMBSMID004I000 / INMBSMID008I000 / INMBSMID032I000 / MD-AC-MBS-4 / MD-AC-MBS-8 / MD-AC-MBS-32, user manual v1.7 EN; up to 4, 8 or 32 indoor units on one XYE bus.",
  "summary": "Modbus RTU slave on the XYE bus of Midea commercial and VRF indoor units. Each of up to 4, 8 or 32 index slots maps to an indoor unit address and has a 20-register block for on/off, mode, fan, vane, setpoint, room temperature, alarm, error and remote lock; registers 0..8 send commands to all units.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Tables give a 'protocol address' and a 'PLC address' (protocol + 1); the protocol address is the wire address. Index n (0..31) uses protocol address 1000 + 20 x n + offset. This file lists n = 0 (1000..1009)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Intesis INMBSMID***I000 Modbus RTU (EIA-485) Interface for Midea air conditioners - User's Manual",
    "doc_number": "User Manual v1.7 EN",
    "revision_date": "2024-08",
    "url": "https://www.hms-networks.com/docs/default-source/products/intesis/manuals-and-guides---manuals/user-manual-inmbsmidxxxi000.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 9-11 (registers), pp. 12-14 (DIP switches)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Every register is a 16-bit unsigned holding register per the manual. Temperature rows print an initialisation value of -32678 (some rows -32768, which is raw 0x8000 = 32768); -32678 looks like a typo for -32768 but the manual does not confirm it, so no marker value is given for those rows.",
    "Temperatures follow DIP switch SW4: whole °C, decidegrees (x10) or °F. The register footnotes call x10 the default, but the SW4 table marks Celsius degrees as the factory setting, so scale 1 / °C is used here; with x10 selected use 0.1.",
    "The baud-rate registers are left out: the manual lists the available rates but not the number that stands for each one.",
    "Only index n = 0 is listed. For index n add 20 x n (n = 1 on/off = 1020).",
    "The index n is not the unit's address in the AC system: write the unit's address (0..63) into 1000 + 20 x n + 9 first.",
    "Error code list not reproduced; see the manual's error-code section."
  ],
